platform/x86: touchscreen_dmi: Add info for the Chuwi Vi8 Plus with unfilled DMI

Some Chuwi Vi8 Plus (CWI519) units leave the SMBIOS system fields at the
placeholder string, reporting "To be filled by O.E.M." for both sys_vendor
and product_name. On those units the existing Vi8 Plus entry cannot match,
so the ICN8505 firmware is never extracted from the EFI image and the
touchscreen does not work.

This is not a factory misprogramming that a BIOS update repairs: the
placeholder is what the firmware image ships. Parsing the SMBIOS defaults
out of the last BIOS Chuwi published for this tablet (P03_C806.109,
2016-02-25) shows "To be filled by O.E.M." for the system manufacturer and
product name, with the board fields correctly set to "Hampoo" and
"Cherry Trail CR".

Add a second entry keyed on the board fields plus the BIOS date, the same
approach already used for the Chuwi HiBook (CWI514) a few entries above.

Signed-off-by: Your Name <your.email@example.com>
---
 Generated against linux master 3eb40771c00a (2026-08-15).
 Apply with: git am, or patch -p1 < this file
---
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/touchscreen_dmi.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/touchscreen_dmi.c
@@ -1236,7 +1236,17 @@
 		.matches = {
 			DMI_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "Hampoo"),
 			DMI_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "D2D3_Vi8A1"),
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "Cherry Trail CR"),
+		},
+	},
+	{
+		/* Chuwi Vi8 Plus (CWI519), unit with unfilled system DMI */
+		.driver_data = (void *)&chuwi_vi8_plus_data,
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_VENDOR, "Hampoo"),
 			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "Cherry Trail CR"),
+			/* Above matches are too generic, add bios-date match */
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BIOS_DATE, "12/11/2015"),
 		},
 	},
 	{
